<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#crucifixion">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Crucifixion</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as crucify</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Crucifixion is a method of execution in which the condemned is fastened to a cross or stake and left to die. It was used in the ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthaginians</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a>, Carthaginian authorities could crucify generals held responsible for military failures.</p></div>
